ad Brighton marmalised the defending Premier League champions. A record crowd of 31,944 were at the Amex Stadium to witness\nFormed in 1901, Brighton were a Southern League club for almost two decades before they were voted into the Football League. They\nSmith, clear on goal with a chance to earn Brighton their first major trophy, saw his shot saved by Manchester United goalkeeper\nGary Bailey. United won the replay. But in 1995, chairman Bill Archer sold Brighton 's Goldstone Ground, their home since 1902, because\nowned the stadium, after the final game of the 1995-96 campaign, which had to be abandoned as thousands of furious fans spilled\nclub returned to the city in 1999 and started playing at Withdean Stadium, most famous for being the home athletics track of\n's current stadium in Falmer. Former chairman Dick Knight stabilised a club that in 1997 came within 27 minutes of being relegated\nHe became chairman in 2009, and masterminded the rise from League One and move into the American Express Stadium. Last season, Brighton\nBrighton batter Arsenal in shock first defeat as champions By Simon Stone Chief football news reporter Published 19 September 2026, 07:30 BST", "retrieved_text_sha256": "8cc42f5a9c6ec2df59034a469bb3b5d1635c98be61d23571cbc253b54755a085"}], "research": {"event_date": "2026-09-19", "sensitive": false, "claims": [{"id": "c1", "fact": "\u0641\u064a \u064a\u0648\u0645 \u0627\u062d\u062a\u0641\u0627\u0644 \u0628\u0631\u0627\u064a\u062a\u0648\u0646 \u0628\u0645\u0631\u0648\u0631 125 \u0633\u0646\u0629 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u062a\u0623\u0633\u064a\u0633\u0647\u060c \u0641\u0627\u0632 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0622\u0631\u0633\u0646\u0627\u0644 \u062d\u0627\u0645\u0644 \u0644\u0642\u0628 \u0627\u0644\u062f\u0648\u0631\u064a \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0646\u062c\u0644\u064a\u0632\u064a 3-0 \u0623\u0645\u0627\u0645 \u062d\u0636\u0648\u0631 \u0642\u064a\u0627\u0633\u064a \u0628\u0644\u063a 31,944 \u0645\u062a\u0641\u0631\u062c\u0627\u064b \u0641\u064a \u0645\u0644\u